Freeciv @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=====================================================

Freeciv is the open-source empire-building strategy game in the manner of
Civilization: found cities, research, trade, make war and peace, from
4000 BC to the space age. This is its AmigaOS 3.x build for a 68040 or
68060 with an FPU: the SDL 2 client (through GFOpenGPU) and the server,
English only. Status: release candidate, not yet a release.

This is the client drawer: the client with the data it plays with (the
classic and civ2civ3 rulesets, the human theme, the trident tileset, the
small flags, and the standard sounds and music) and the server it starts
for a game on this Amiga. Freeciv's other tilesets, themes, scenarios,
large flags and translations are not in it; they are to come later as an
archive of their own.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board,
  and plenty of fast RAM (the client alone used about 45 MB).
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module, SDL2_image.module and SDL2_mixer.module in
  LIBS:GFOpenGPU/ (the Installer copies one there from LIBS:OpenGPU/
  where only that folder has it).
- bsdsocket.library (GFOpenSocket): the client talks to its own server
  on this machine.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive anywhere (lha x freeciv-...lha RAM:) and run
Install-Freeciv from its icon. It checks the CPU, the FPU and the modules,
asks where the Freeciv drawer should go (Work:Games is offered), and
copies it there. Settings and saves go to the drawer's User drawer; an
update leaves User as it is. Copying the Freeciv drawer and its icon
yourself works too.

Playing
-------

- Double-click Freeciv (the client; its icon gives it the large stack it
  needs). "Start New Game" starts the server beside it.
- From a Shell: cd to the drawer, then Stack 1000000 and Freeciv. With no
  options it uses the trident tileset this archive holds and plays sound
  through AHI; Freeciv -t trident -P none plays without sound.
- Shift+Return ends a turn. Options, Save Game and Load Game are in the
  client's menu; Options, Quit closes the client and the server with it.

Licence
-------

Freeciv and its data are GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING); the source is at
https://github.com/freeciv/freeciv. The icons are drawn from Freeciv's own
client icon.

